    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d871-a1">

                <pb facs="0695" n="613" sameAs="frus:frus1911/pg613"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary for Foreign
                            Affairs to the American
                        Ambassador.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1911-05-10"><hi rendition="#italic">May 10,
                        1911</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Ambassador</hi>: In reply to your excellency’s
                    note No. 519A-332 of the 24th of April last, relative to the liberty of the
                    American citizens Converse, Blatt and Brown, I have the honor to inform you that
                    by virtue of the authority conferred upon the Government by the first part of
                    article 190 of the Penal Code of the Federal district, it has been determined,
                    to expel them from the Republic.</p>
                <p>Inclosed herewith is a copy of said article.</p>
                <p>I avail [etc.],</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">F. L. de la
                    Barra.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
